{
    "background_story": "Amaia was a young and ambitious farmer who had just inherited her family's rural land. Determined to restore the farm to its former glory, she spent every waking moment tending to the crops. One day, while harvesting the oat fields, Amaia stumbled upon an old, forgotten technique for using haulm - the dry leaves and stalks of the oats - as a natural fertilizer. Intrigued, she began experimenting with the method, carefully collecting and composting the haulm to create a nutrient-rich soil amendment. As the seasons passed, Amaia's crops began to flourish, and her farm became renowned for its exceptional produce. News of her innovative approach spread, and soon, other farmers were seeking her advice on how to harness the power of haulm. Amaia's dedication to sustainable farming practices had not only revitalized her family's land but also earned her a reputation as a pioneer in her field.",
